  78:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *
  79:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** * Description: This function is called by your application code to create a timer.
  80:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *
  81:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** * Arguments  : dly           Initial delay.
  82:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *                            If the timer is configured for ONE-SHOT mode, this is the timeout used
  83:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *                            If the timer is configured for PERIODIC mode, this is the first timeou
  84:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *                               wait for before the timer starts entering periodic mode.
  85:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *
  86:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *              period        The 'period' being repeated for the timer.
  87:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *                               If you specified 'OS_TMR_OPT_PERIODIC' as an option, when the timer
  88:./ucos/Core/os_tmr.c **** *                               expires, it will automatically restart with the same period.
